+The initial integrated native run passed 39 of 48 cases. Nine foliage bounds assertions failed, including the neutral frame. A distinct one-case diagnosis kept the old assertion and recorded both methods. Rotated local bbox corners reported -0.140094 art units, while exact transformed cubic and quadratic path extrema reported +4.490977 units for the same leaves. The box included empty corners. The final method minimizes every actual cubic, quadratic and closing-line path along both fixed authored art axes, with actual per-path stroke widths and uniform local/art matrix scale. Bounds and tolerances remain unchanged. Coarse bbox values remain diagnostic metadata. No production art or motion changed to satisfy this correction. Both failed harness versions are archived.
+
+The first green integrated run passed all 48 cases in 87.280788114 seconds. It measured seven phases across three species and two rotations, checked root attachment and painted curve bounds, native timing and completion, coalescing, deadlines, live system/device/cross-tab reduction, player interruption and unchanged saved tables. Its first-green stills sampled the CSS peak while the resident fake clock was near action entry. They are retained foliage evidence, not same-phase character captures. The refined final captures advance the resident fake clock to the same 280 ms phase, record actual last RAF time and body transform, and require alignment within one 16 ms frame. This instrumentation is test-only and uses a distinct capture directory.
